# ── Scraper OUTPUT ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-state output folders (gaps, stats-tab, box scores, accumulated, Final).
# These are generated data, not source — the full set runs to several GB and
# individual files can exceed GitHub's 100 MB hard limit.
*_scraped_data/
*_Scraped_data/
Final_scraped_data/
scraper_output/
stats_only_check/

# Output files, wherever they land
*_data_gaps_*.json
*_box_scores_*.json
*_accumulated_stats_*.json
*_all_stats_tab_*.json
Final_*_accumulated_*.json
missing_teams_*.json
*_anomalies.json
completely_missing_teams_*.csv
high_school_missing_teams_*.xlsx

# Intermediate team lists (regenerated by state_teams_counter.py).
# NOTE: the master lists boys/girls_basketball_all_states[_YY-YY].json ARE
# tracked — the scraper needs them at runtime to enumerate teams and to
# resolve opponents to canonical names.
boys_basketball_teams_list.json
girls_basketball_teams_list.json

# Archives
*.zip

# Personal scratch notes
instructions.txt

# Ad-hoc debug scripts (kept locally, not part of the pipeline)
_*.py
diagnose_box_score_blank.py
fetch_via_chrome.py

# Reference drop from the second machine: keep the scraper/README for
# provenance, skip its copies of files we already track (the two
# *_all_states.json master lists are byte-identical to the tracked ones,
# ~19 MB of duplication) and its scraped test output.
